PHASE 2 – TECHNOLOGY CHOICES

HTML

HTML is used to create the structure and content of the Library Book Checkout System. It is used for pages such as the Dashboard, Books, Checkout, Return, and Users pages.


CSS

CSS is used to design and style the user interface. It controls the layout, colors, spacing, tables, buttons, forms, and responsive appearance of the system.


JavaScript

JavaScript is used to provide the functionality of the Library Book Checkout System. It handles book checkout, book return, user information, book availability, and other system interactions.


localStorage

Browser localStorage is used as the data storage mechanism for the prototype. It allows the system to save books, users, and checkout information within the browser.


Visual Studio Code

Visual Studio Code is used as the development environment for creating and editing the project files.


Live Server

Live Server is used to run the HTML-based prototype locally during development and testing.


Technology Limitation

The current prototype is a client-side application and does not use a centralized backend database. Because of this, the stored localStorage data is limited to the browser where the application is being used.

For a production system, a backend server and centralized database would be recommended together with appropriate authentication, authorization, validation, encryption, and logging controls.